            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.679,
            0.464,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Bridging Science and Society"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.706,
            0.888,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some infectious diseases are caused by parasitic worms. They enter our bodies through contaminated water and food. They live inside our body, especially in the alimentary canal (the digestive system). These worms take nutrients from our body and live like parasites (the organism that lives in or on another organism is called the host). For this reason, it is suggested to wash your hands properly, maintain personal hygiene and good sanitary habits, consume properly cooked food and boiled or filtered drinking water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.847,
            0.713,
            0.885
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Nematoda (roundworms) — Efficient body design with two openings"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.887,
            0.776,
            0.94
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Roundworms have elongated, cylindrical bodies (Fig. 12.16d). This body structure allows their efficient movement through soil, water, or host tissues. This body form increases the range of environment in which"
            }
          ]
        }
